cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Wenuray in your research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: "Wenuray: radio-interferometric self-calibration"
abstract: >-
  Wenuray is a Python framework for radio-interferometric self-calibration on top of CASA. A
  self-calibration procedure is described once, as a short TOML recipe or a few Python objects,
  and checked against self-calibration theory before it runs. Imaging is pluggable: CASA tclean,
  Pyralysis or a user's own imager. Every run records the resolved recipe and its provenance, so
  it can be repeated exactly.
